{% import "partials/copy-command.njk" as cmd %}
{% import "partials/zoomable-image.njk" as media %}

<h1>Getting started</h1>
<p>Install the controller and run your first test. Complete the
  <a class="text-accent" href="/setup/prerequisites/">Prerequisites</a> first.</p>

<h2 id="install-controller">Install the controller</h2>

<h3 id="install-from-pypi">Install from PyPI</h3>
<p>If the controller machine is connected to the internet, install Orcraft from PyPI:</p>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>OS</th>
      <th>Command</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td>Windows</td>
      <td>{{ cmd.copyCell("pip install orcraft") }}</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Linux, macOS</td>
      <td>{{ cmd.copyCell("pip3 install orcraft") }}</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
<p>Installing into a virtual environment is recommended, and required on distributions that
  protect the system Python - see
  <a class="text-accent" href="/setup/prerequisites/#virtual-environment">Prerequisites/Virtual environment</a>.</p>

<h3 id="install-from-a-wheel-file">Install from a wheel file</h3>
<p>If the machine has no internet access, download the wheel on a connected machine, copy it over
  and install it directly:</p>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>OS</th>
      <th>Command</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td>Windows</td>
      <td>{{ cmd.copyCell("pip install orcraft-<version>-py3-none-any.whl") }}</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Linux, macOS</td>
      <td>{{ cmd.copyCell("pip3 install orcraft-<version>-py3-none-any.whl") }}</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2 id="run-controller">Run the controller</h2>
{{ cmd.copyCommand("orcraft-controller run") }}

<h2 id="run-the-test">Run the test</h2>

<h3 id="clone-tutorial">Clone the tutorial suite</h3>
<p>Clone the Orcraft Tutorial repository, which contains a ready-to-run "Hello World" test:</p>
{{ cmd.copyCommand("git clone https://github.com/GMCoreAI/orcraft-test-suite-tutorial.git") }}
<p class="text-danger">This repository is currently private; the link above will be updated once it is public.</p>

<h3 id="add-the-suite">Add the suite</h3>
<ol>
  <li>In the controller, click <strong class="text-cyan">Add Item</strong> to add the tutorial suite to the session.</li>
</ol>
{{ media.zoomableImage("/assets/images/screenshots/setup/getting-started/add-suite.png", "The controller with an empty session: the Add Item button in the Session frame and the Add Item placeholder row in the tree", "large") }}
<ol start="2">
  <li>Select the cloned tutorial suite's entry point Python file.</li>
</ol>
{{ media.zoomableImage("/assets/images/screenshots/setup/getting-started/select-tutorial-suite-file.png", "The Add Item file dialog open on the orcraft-test-suite-tutorial folder with test_suite_tutorial.py entered as the file name", "large") }}

<h3 id="select-the-test">Select the test</h3>
<p>Click on the <strong>Hello World</strong> test.</p>
{{ media.zoomableImage("/assets/images/screenshots/setup/getting-started/hello-world-test.png", "The execution tree with the tutorial suite loaded and the Hello World test row selected", "large") }}

<h3 id="start-the-run">Start the run</h3>
<ol>
  <li>Click <strong class="text-purple">Run</strong> in the configuration panel on the right side.</li>
</ol>
{{ media.zoomableImage("/assets/images/screenshots/setup/getting-started/click-run.png", "The configuration panel of the Hello World test with its Cycles field and the Run button at the bottom right", "large") }}
<ol start="2">
  <li>Confirm the run.</li>
</ol>
{{ media.zoomableImage("/assets/images/screenshots/setup/getting-started/confirm-run.png", "The Confirm Run dialog saying this will run 1 test case in 1 test, with Yes and No buttons", "large") }}

<h3 id="check-the-result">Check the result</h3>
<p>Follow the test log as it executes.</p>
{{ media.zoomableImage("/assets/images/screenshots/common/test-log.png", "The controller after the run: the Hello World run row with a Pass status in the tree, its log in the right pane and the Execution Status frame at 100 percent", "large") }}

<p>A <strong class="text-success">Pass</strong> result confirms that the Orcraft Test Framework is available for
  developing tests, and that local runs already work as expected.</p>
<p>If you're only interested in local runs, proceed to the <a class="text-accent" href="/tutorial/">Tutorial</a>.
  Otherwise, continue to <a class="text-accent" href="/setup/endpoints/">Adding endpoints</a> to distribute test
  execution across machines.</p>
